[1] P(T=n) anchors are proved by a SEPARATE elementary argument in
    each front (D2.1/D3.1/D4.1), not via the CDF polynomial at k=n.
    (k=n is outside the polynomial's proved domain 0<=k<=n-1.)
    Cited only, not re-checked here (would require re-deriving the
    elementary argument itself, out of scope).

[2] Mean recovery via tail-sum identity: E[n*M_n^(K)] =
    sum_{k=0}^{n-1} P(n*M_n^(K) > k) = sum_{k=0}^{n-1} [1-CDF(k)]
    Compare n*phi_n^(K) against cited finite-n mean formulas.
    K=2: n*E[M_n^(2)] via tail-sum = n - (2*n - 3)*(n**2/2 - n/2)/(n**3 - n**2) + (n**5/5 - n**4/2 + n**3/3 - n/30)/(n**4 - n**3) - (2*n - 1)*(n**3/3 - n**2/2 + n/6)/n**3
           => E[M_n^(2)] = (16*n**3 + n**2 + 21*n + 6)/(30*n**3)
           n->oo limit = 8/15
    K=3: n*E[M_n^(3)] via tail-sum = n + (2*n - 3)*(n**4/4 - n**3/2 + n**2/4)/(n**6 - 3*n**5 + 2*n**4) + (n**2/2 - n/2)*(-3*n**3 + 12*n**2 - 12*n - 2)/(n**5 - 3*n**4 + 2*n**3) + (3*n**2 - 9*n - 1)*(n**5/5 - n**4/2 + n**3/3 - n/30)/(n**6 - 3*n**5 + 2*n**4) + (n**3/3 - n**2/2 + n/6)*(-3*n**4 + 12*n**3 - 15*n**2 + 9*n + 2)/(n**6 - 3*n**5 + 2*n**4) + 3*(n**6/6 - n**5/2 + 5*n**4/12 - n**2/12)/(n**6 - 3*n**5 + 2*n**4) - (n**7/7 - n**6/2 + n**5/2 - n**3/6 + n/42)/(n**6 - 3*n**5 + 2*n**4)
           => E[M_n^(3)] = (32*n**4 + 5*n**3 + 77*n**2 + 46*n + 12)/(70*n**4)
           n->oo limit = 16/35
    K=4: n*E[M_n^(4)] via tail-sum = n - (n**2/2 - n/2)*(4*n**5 - 30*n**4 + 74*n**3 - 52*n**2 - 30*n - 12)/(n**7 - 6*n**6 + 11*n**5 - 6*n**4) - (-12*n**2 + 62*n + 20)*(n**6/6 - n**5/2 + 5*n**4/12 - n**2/12)/(n**8 - 6*n**7 + 11*n**6 - 6*n**5) - (4*n**2 - 18*n - 22)*(n**7/7 - n**6/2 + n**5/2 - n**3/6 + n/42)/(n**8 - 6*n**7 + 11*n**6 - 6*n**5) - (n**3/3 - n**2/2 + n/6)*(4*n**6 - 30*n**5 + 80*n**4 - 102*n**3 + 67*n**2 + 58*n + 12)/(n**8 - 6*n**7 + 11*n**6 - 6*n**5) - (n**4/4 - n**3/2 + n**2/4)*(-8*n**3 + 42*n**2 - 50*n - 28)/(n**8 - 6*n**7 + 11*n**6 - 6*n**5) - (n**5/5 - n**4/2 + n**3/3 - n/30)*(-6*n**4 + 42*n**3 - 71*n**2 - 40*n + 11)/(n**8 - 6*n**7 + 11*n**6 - 6*n**5) - 8*(n**8/8 - n**7/2 + 7*n**6/12 - 7*n**4/24 + n**2/12)/(n**8 - 6*n**7 + 11*n**6 - 6*n**5) + (n**9/9 - n**8/2 + 2*n**7/3 - 7*n**5/15 + 2*n**3/9 - n/30)/(n**8 - 6*n**7 + 11*n**6 - 6*n**5)
           => E[M_n^(4)] = (256*n**5 + 69*n**4 + 964*n**3 + 891*n**2 + 490*n + 120)/(630*n**5)
           n->oo limit = 128/315

